user_prompt_template:
UPSTREAM TUTORIAL FRAMING:
{upstream_system_architecture}

PROJECT CONTEXT:
Tutorial Request: {topic}
Skill Level: {skill_level}
Tutorial Type: {tutorial_type}
Stack: {stack}
Depth: {depth}
Include Code: {include_code}
Output Style: {output_style}
Constraints: {constraints}
Audience: {audience}
Tone: {tone}

Produce the master tutorial outline. One chapter per module from the upstream framing, in build order. Each chapter must include a worksheet plan with 2–4 checkpoint/exercise sheets.

For the worksheet plan, mix sheet types across each chapter: aim for one reference-style sheet (table — commands, config values, file map, or API endpoints), one verification checklist (how to confirm the step worked), and 0–2 exercise or planning sheets (form). Do not repeat the same sheet type more than twice in a single chapter.

Before finalising each title, ask: could this title appear unchanged in a completely different tutorial? If yes, rewrite it until it cannot.

Return ONLY the following JSON object. No prose. No markdown. No code fences.

{{
  "document_title": "Full tutorial title naming the exact outcome and stack — e.g. 'Build and Deploy a SaaS Landing Page with Next.js and Tailwind'",
  "document_subtitle": "A hands-on walkthrough for [specific audience and goal] — not a generic tagline",
  "system_name": "Exact system_name from upstream framing",
  "version": "1.0",
  "total_chapters": 0,
  "master_operating_rules": [
    "[Specific working convention for this tutorial] — Rationale: [why it exists for this stack]. Trigger: [when it applies]. Risk: [the concrete error or time cost of ignoring it]."
  ],
  "cascade_chain": [
    {{
      "source_domain": "Module name from upstream framing",
      "triggers": ["Module name that depends on it"],
      "condition": "When [specific output or verification in source module] is done, it unblocks [specific action in the dependent module]"
    }}
  ],
  "disclaimer_required": false,
  "introduction_text": "2–3 sentence overview specific to this tutorial — what the reader will build, who it is for, and what they will be able to do at the end",
  "chapters": [
    {{
      "chapter_number": 1,
      "domain_id": "domain-01",
      "domain_name": "Must match upstream module name exactly",
      "chapter_title": "Specific step title naming what gets built or accomplished — not a phase or overview. Must be specific enough that it could not appear unchanged in a different tutorial.",
      "chapter_purpose": "One sentence: what the learner can do after completing this step that they could not do before",
      "key_topics": [
        "Specific topic derived from the upstream module scope — must name an actual command, file, API, concept, or decision involved in this step"
      ],
      "common_gap": "The single most common and costly mistake learners make in this exact step — name the mechanism and the observable symptom",
      "cascade_triggers": [
        "When [specific output or verification in this chapter] is done, it unblocks [specific action] in [named module]"
      ],
      "worksheet_plan": [
        {{
          "worksheet_id": "ws-01-a",
          "title": "Specific checkpoint/exercise/reference sheet title naming the verification or output it enables — cannot be generic",
          "purpose": "One sentence: the specific verification, reference, or practice output this sheet produces",
          "section_count": 3,
          "estimated_field_count": 12
        }}
      ]
    }}
  ]
}}
